ted him digitally surprisingly he  did no filming for those final moments  instead they added him into the scene  using cgi when he made his comeback in  spider-man no way home he also got some  digital reconstruction done they de-aged  him  before bella can even transition into a  vampire she has another ironically much  more lethal transition the filmmakers  needed to showcase how much her  pregnancy with renesme took out of her  this translated into making it look like  kristen stewart had dropped at least 30  pounds  you look terrible while prosthetics did  help them out a little it was only with  the final touches of cgi on her face and  entire body that they were able to  create what we see in breaking dawn part  one  peace  we're going to let you in on a secret  robert downey jr isn't a superhero in  real life which means he's also not  invincible for example rdj hurt his  ankle so bad on the set of iron man 3  that he was out of production for a full  six weeks but instead of halting filming  and delaying the release date marvel put  the film in the hands of the visual  effects department who were able to take  footage of an rdj body double and  digitally recreate and insert rdj's face  in post-production you know the iconic i  am iron man speech that wasn't really  rdj i'm a changed man no one could ever  guess just how successful twilight was  going to be so naturally a lot of things  changed when they got the ok to film the  rest of the saga things like a bigger  budget and a very different location for  new moon production was moved from  portland to vancouver but they had to  somehow keep the continuity between the  two films especially with the buildings  to do this they basically reconstructed  forks high using a green screen the  actors were actually just filming in an  outdoor parking lot  although the philosopher's stone was  made back in 2001 they were still able  to pull off some major cgi that you  probably didn't even notice during the  quidditch match in this film almost half  of the students on the broom were added  into the scene solely using cgi there  were no live actors for them filming  while it isn't the most perfect visual  effects we have to give them credit for  how seamlessly they added it in  scared harry  a little we've all seen enough of the  behind the scenes of spider-man to know  that tom holland does in fact wear a  physical spidey suit however a lot goes  into that suit to make it movie ready  using cgi they make sure that any seams  zippers wrinkles and creases are  invisible at all times during the film  even when he's just walking around that  way he always looks flawless although  brief captain marvel's appearance in  avengers end game was nothing short of  epic her hair blowing in that space wind  while her suit glows iconic but what if  we told you her hair wasn't actually  real yup brie larson actually wore a  head cap while filming this scene every  strand of hair we see in this moment was  digitally recreated and can we just say  wow it's just him  watching thor lose his eye in ragnarok  wasn't easy but filming with an eye  patch during infinity war was even  harder for chris hemsworth the eye patch  prop would constantly slip off his face  while filming until they decided they  would digitally add the eye patch in  using cgi luckily they didn't have to do  this for long thanks to rocket's slight  obsession with artificial body parts  what's this what's it look like  we all suspected that the black  panther's suit had some type of cgi  effect how else would it literally glow  purple however that wasn't all they used  cgi on the suit for while chadwick  boseman and his stunt doubles did wear a  physical suit a lot of visual effects  went into making sure it was seamless  and to give it its very sleek and  out-of-this-world appearance including  the facial part of the costume that was  often added in during post-production as  well  turns out it wasn't just captain  marvel's hair that needed some cgi  intervention during end game originally  captain marvel was meant to have the  same suit in both her film and end game  but when someone pointed out that all  the other heroes changed their outfits  every few years captain marvel's 25-year  run with the suit didn't seem realistic  so they enhanced brie larson's costume  to look completely different in  post-production  despite what you might have thought the  wolf of wall street included some major  digital enhancements including this  tennis court scene the scene was pieced  together using real life reference the  digital recreation of the buildings as  well as having the actors film in front  of a green screen and adding them into  the scenery in post-production it's no  comparison to an epic magical battle but  it's subtle and impressive nonetheless  les miz was given credit for being a  cinematic masterpiece and a part of this  praise came with the fact that the  actors were actually singing live while  filming this meant they were constantly  all wearing earpieces and microphones of  course it wouldn't have been realistic  or logical to have this technology  visible in the actual film this posed a  great challenge in post-production whose  job it was to use cgi to edit out all  the earpieces and microphones from each  actor have you spotted any forgotten  earpieces  the cgi used on natalie portman's hand  in the black swan is almost undetectable  and honestly extremely impressive which  is what makes it so great to reflect  natalie portman's character very  vigorous training and dedication they  used cgi to make the actresses fingers  smaller and more elongated  cgi isn't always about the explosions  and car chases but the subtle details  that we don't always notice however  without these nuances we wouldn't have  the perfections of super suits but the  idea is to not be noticed or the realism  of hair blowing in the wind which subtle  cgi moment was your favorite can you  think of any o